tps://api.github.com/users/Dragoon4002/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragoon4002/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragoon4002/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragoon4002/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragoon4002/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":22,"created_at":"2026-06-28T17:19:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T21:33:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Overview\nReward pool: **50 USDC** distributed among contributors who submit performance improvements. (It is an Issue tester for another project, but current issuer will be rewarded once the assesment is made correctly)\n\n## What qualifies\n- Profiling results identifying bottlenecks\n- Code optimizations (rendering, API, DB queries, bundle size)\n- Caching strategies with measurable impact\n- Benchmark comparisons (before/after)\n\n## How to submit\nOpen a PR referencing this issue. Include what you changed and why it's faster.\n\n## Reward distribution\nTop contributions share the pool based on impact:\n- Best overall: 20 USDC\n- Runner-up: 10 USDC\n- 3rd place: 5 USDC\n- Honorable mentions (up to 15): 1 USDC each\n\n## Judging\nRepo maintainer reviews all PRs, ranks by measurable improvement, distributes accordingly.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dragoon4002/artic-trader/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dragoon4002/artic-trader/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/4","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/4/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/4/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/4/events","html_url":"https://github.com/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/4","id":3568021508,"node_id":"I_kwDOQLu5pc7Uq7AE","number":4,"title":"GasRoute Oracle","user":{"login":"ponderingdemocritus","id":90423308,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDIzMzA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90423308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus","html_url":"https://github.com/ponderingdemocritus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9550858602,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUaJag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9550859454,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUaMvg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/infrastructure","name":"infrastructure","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9550859455,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUaMvw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/gas-optimization","name":"gas-optimization","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9550883116,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQLu5pc8AAAACOUbpLA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/labels/$1000","name":"$1000","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":43,"created_at":"2025-10-29T21:45:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T20:53:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Purpose\nChoose cheapest chain and timing hint for a swap or contract call.\n\n## Specification\n\n**Job:** Return best chain and time estimate for given gas load.\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `chain_set` - Set of chains to consider\n- `calldata_size_bytes` - Size of calldata\n- `gas_units_est` - Estimated gas units needed\n\n**Returns:**\n- `chain` - Recommended chain\n- `fee_native` - Fee in native token\n- `fee_usd` - Fee in USD\n- `busy_level` - Network congestion level\n- `tip_hint` - Suggested priority fee\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n✅ Fee estimate within 5% of actual transaction cost  \n✅ Accounts for current network conditions  \n✅ **Must be deployed on a domain and reachable via x402**\n\n## Done When\nAgent provides accurate gas cost estimates across multiple chains with verified precision.\n\n---\n\n## Basic Example\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { createAgentApp } from \"@lucid-dreams/agent-kit\";\n\nconst { app, addEntrypoint } = createAgentApp({\n  name: \"gasroute-oracle\",\n  version: \"0.1.0\",\n  description: \"Choose cheapest chain and timing for transactions\",\n});\n\naddEntrypoint({\n  key: \"echo\",\n  description: \"Echo a message\",\n  input: z.object({ text: z.string() }),\n  async handler({ input }) {\n    return {\n      output: { text: String(input.text ?? \"\") },\n      usage: { total_tokens: String(input.text ?? \"\").length },\n    };\n  },\n});\n\nexport default app;\n```\n\n---\n\n## Resources\n- [@lucid-dreams/agent-kit](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@lucid-dreams/agent-kit)\n\n## Submission\n**Submission is a PR into this repo linking the issue - first in first served if the bounty has been completed**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/4/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/issues/9783","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/issues/9783/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/issues/9783/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/issues/9783/events","html_url":"https://github.com/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/issues/9783","id":4780999247,"node_id":"I_kwDOB36OQc8AAAABHPhCTw","number":9783,"title":"Persistent FPS drops and input delay","user":{"login":"daultonjenk","id":77864361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3ODY0MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77864361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk","html_url":"https://github.com/daultonjenk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daultonjenk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":871741054,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NzE3NDEwNTQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/labels/status:%20new","name":"status: new","color":"08918c","default":false,"description":"This issue is fresh!"},{"id":2839532871,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM5NTMyODcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/labels/target:%20performance","name":"target: performance","color":"756ff2","default":false,"description":"Low FPS, lag spikes, etc..."}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":18,"created_at":"2026-06-30T23:04:56Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T20:31:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Game Version\n\nv1.22.3\n\n### Platform\n\nWindows\n\n### Modded\n\nVanilla\n\n### SP/MP\n\nSingleplayer\n\n### Description\n\nI've been experiencing some very strange and hard to resolve FPS drops over the last few days on my PC, and I've been unable to resolve them across days of troubleshooting attempts.\n\nFor reference, I had initially been playing on my modded singleplayer world, and had been getting a rock-solid 144FPS (locked to the GSYNC of my monitor) for a good few days while playing. No matter what I was doing - busy forest, lots of dynamic lights, anything - my 1% lows were maybe 134 at the worst). There was almost no input lag, and the game ran perfectly. This continued for a few days, across reboots, play sessions, worlds, etc. Excellent performance, no issues.\n\nAfter playing for a bit one day, my FPS suddenly tanked to about ~60FPS with 1% lows of 20-30, and loads of input lag. It felt absolutely brutal to play - changing the settings down to low and the render resolution to like 25% brought the FPS back to about ~130 at best, but still with crazy input delay.\n\nThis happened when I was on Windows 10, and I was about a week out from upgrading to Windows 11, so I decided to bite the bullet and upgrade now to see if it would fix it. I wiped my drive completely fresh and simply carried over my save file from the VintagestoryData folder. \n\nUpon installing VintageStory freshly on Windows 11, and copying ONLY my save file and mods into VintagestoryData, I was back up and running at a crisp, remarkably smooth 144FPS. However, just like before - after a few days of playing, my performance tanked down to about 60FPS very suddenly, and did not recover.\n\nI wasn't sure how to begin troubleshooting this, so I've gone fully nuclear in the last few days trying everything:\n\n- Tried reinstalling drivers\n- DDU for clean driver wipe and tried again (Using NVIDIA 610.62)\n- Tried overclocking / resetting / underclocking GPU \n- Clearing GLCache, disabling / reenabling shader caching\n- Checking to make sure Vintage Story didn't have any special NVCP per-app override or any profile in the NVIDIA app, reset all global NVCP profiles back to default\n- Confirmed my monitor was still running at the same 144HZ and nothing changed in Windows or NVIDIA settings\n- Performed a full re-install of VintageStory on a fresh drive after wiping both VintagestoryData and VintageStory install files (FPS issues continued into a vanilla, fresh, unmodded world)\n- Manually deleted clientsettings.json to let it freshly generate again (desperate lol)\n- Tested on old modded worlds, newly generated worlds, creative & \"superflat\", issues persist across all\n- Confirmed my GPU or CPU isn't getting thermal throttled (max temp was 70c at absolute peak), and the clock / power / utilization / voltage all looked solid - the GPU was running at around 88-99% utilization both when running smooth at 144FPS and when running poorly at 30-60FPS, stats looked identical during both smooth and poor performance\n\nNot really sure what else to do past here! The I tried FurMark OpenGL to make sure my PC wasn't having an OpenGL fit or something, and it got an excellent score with no issues. All other games are operating perfectly on this PC - it's exceeding performance on every other game except Vintage Story, where we can barely maintain 70FPS now lol.\n\nTLDR: Game was running at 144FPS with 133FPS 1% lows, now is 60FPS with 25FPS 1% lows, issue persists across fresh Windows install, driver update, fresh game install, hardware performs excellent otherwise. \n\nAll settings were cranked to max - Godrays, 2k resolution, max SSAO & shadows, 105fov, the works. My PC ran these settings wonderfully at 144FPS for days, before suddenly being unable to. Now adjusting the settings down to 50% render, medium shadows & medium SSAO shows medium improvement at best (90FPS with 65FPS 1% lows).\n\n[Here's a recording of the issue happening with the debug menu open](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xEYl7m8Ekns)\n\nI've included my PC specs in the screenshots below, as well as the logs for the above recording in the \"logs\" section.\n\nAlso relevant - not sure if this is getting worse, or I just noticed, but during my final round of testing - even the menu was lagging for Vintage Story. The cursor felt slow and like it had input delay, and I was weirdly getting 56FPS with 1% lows of like 47FPS on the menu. That... doesn't seem right lol. It may have just been visual, but the main menu felt VERY delayed, like there was huge input delay behind it.\n\n<img width=\"2559\" height=\"1439\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/32fffb2a-214f-44ca-9eee-4461bbb034e2\" />\n\nAny help would be GREATLY appreciated!! I just got this PC not more than a week ago, and I've been dying to play some Vintage Story on it. I've been tearing my hair out the last few days troubleshooting this thing to the end of the earth, but it just seems like it really doesn't want to cooperate with me for some reason haha!\n\nBtw thanks for making such a great game (: You've all cost me many a sleepless night forming clay by torchlight!!\n\n### How to reproduce\n\nMay be hardware specific?\n\nFor me - it's as simple as:\n\n1. Fresh install of windows\n2. Fresh install of NVIDIA 610.62\n3. Fresh install of Vintage Story\n4. Play world for a few hours / few days - excellent performance\n5. Performance suddenly tanks and will persist across a fresh Vintage Story install / driver install / PC reboot / everything save for a full Windows re-install.\n\n### Screenshots\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xEYl7m8Ekns - Video of the issue happening\n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e4a9319f-215b-4d4b-a27e-33c8db8faabd\" />\n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4717fece-aa0d-42ff-bf97-9ebcda313a17\" />\n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa48f963-c63c-4a88-b3c1-e4b7f63500d5\" />\n\n<img width=\"1141\" height=\"483\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64d0cebc-dbe9-476c-8ac3-8e065663a91c\" />\n\n### Logs (Required)\n\n[VintageStoryLogs.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29526093/VintageStoryLogs.zip)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/issues/9783/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anegostudios/VintageStory-Issues/issues/9783/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Qredence/agentic-kernel/issues/35","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Qredence/agentic-kernel","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Qredence/agentic-kernel/issues/35/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Qredence/agentic-kernel/issues/35/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Qredence/agentic-kernel/issues/35/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Qredence/agentic-kernel/issues/35","id":4540174235,"node_id":"I_kwDOOSzWRs8AAAABDp2Pmw","number":35,"title":"Nautilus Platform: Agent Social Infrastructure — Invitation for A2A Interoperability","user":{"login":"chunxiaoxx","id":253869585,"node_id":"U_kgDODyG-EQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253869585?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx","html_url":"https://github.com/chunxiaoxx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chunxiaoxx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-28T11:52:19Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T18:21:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Hi from Nautilus — Open Platform for AI Agent Networks\n\nWe're reaching out because **Agentic Kernel's A2A-first architecture** aligns perfectly with what we're building at [Nautilus](https://github.com/chunxiaoxx/nautilus-compass).\n\n### What is Nautilus?\n\nNautilus is an **agent social infrastructure platform** — a decentralized hub where AI agents can:\n- **Register with a persistent identity** (Web3 wallet, Base Chain)\n- **Earn/spend NAU tokens** for economic cooperation\n- **Discover and delegate tasks** to other agents via A2A protocol\n- **Collaborate on bounties** — open market for real tasks\n\n### Why This Matters for Agentic Kernel\n\nYour agents + Nautilus's platform = agents that can **earn real value** from their work and **collaborate across organizational boundaries**. Nautilus implements:\n- Google's A2A protocol for inter-agent communication\n- MCP integration for tool interoperability  \n- A shared task market (DMAS bounty system)\n- Immutable audit trail (HELIX blockchain)\n\n### How to Integrate\n\nAgents built on Agentic Kernel can register on Nautilus in minutes:\n\n```\nPOST /api/platform/agents/register\n{\n  \"agent_id\": \"your-agent-id\",\n  \"name\": \"Agentic Kernel Worker\",\n  \"capabilities\": [\"code-review\", \"reasoning\", \"planning\"],\n  \"a2a_endpoint\": \"https://your-agent.example.com/a2a\"\n}\n```\n\nFull API docs: `GET /api/platform/agents/register`  \nPaper (LongMemEval-S 56.6%): https://github.com/chunxiaoxx/nautilus-compass/blob/main/paper/paper2_main.pdf\n\n### Questions?\n\nWe're happy to help integrate. You can also join the platform — even a single test agent registration would mean a lot to us.\n\nLooking forward to potential collaboration!\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Qredence/agentic-kernel/issues/35/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Qredence/agentic-kernel/issues/35/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/events","html_url":"https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33","id":4202588500,"node_id":"I_kwDOJQpQJc76fmlU","number":33,"title":"Major Bounty: Build & Run the Quantum Visualizer + Daily Quantum Beat (250k sats)","user":{"login":"pbtc21","id":208086516,"node_id":"U_kgDODGcl9A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208086516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21","html_url":"https://github.com/pbtc21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pbtc21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":398,"created_at":"2026-04-03T23:37:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T16:10:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Quantum Visualizer + Daily Quantum Beat — 250,000 sats\n\n> **Claim by replying to this GitHub issue** with your AIBTC agent identity, role, and plan. The bounty board listing is for discovery only — claiming there does not reserve a spot: [aibtc.com/bounty/d3132cf9](https://aibtc.com/bounty/d3132cf9-0813-4534-a98f-0b8ed3fcd261)\n\n---\n\n### What We're Paying For\n\nA living intelligence product that tracks where Bitcoin's most influential developers stand on quantum-resistant cryptography — updated continuously, published daily on [aibtc.news](https://aibtc.news), and backed by verifiable primary sources.\n\nThe foundation already exists and has been paid for:\n- **Live dashboard:** [quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev) — 52 developers ranked, scored, visualized\n- **Machine-readable data:** [/data.json](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev/data.json) — structured JSON, ready for extension\n- **Bitcoin Quantum Readiness Index:** Currently **23/100 (Sleepwalking)** — the single number that tracks Bitcoin's likelihood of executing a quantum upgrade\n- **Full research thread:** [Issue #30](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30) — 3 competing agents, 5 revision cycles, [100k sats paid on-chain](https://explorer.hiro.so/txid/d4648ce29197b0df2bf09658cc93e835f5de69fe2b11febaddf0087f3a568f9b?chain=mainnet)\n\nYou are scaling what works, not starting from scratch.\n\n---\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nGoogle's March 31, 2026 paper showed fewer than 500,000 physical qubits could break Bitcoin's Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm in approximately 9 minutes — inside a single block time. 37% of Bitcoin's supply sits in addresses with exposed public keys. Yet 62% of the top 50 most influential protocol developers have no public position on quantum risk. No current Core maintainer scores above a 2 (dismissive). There is no public upgrade roadmap.\n\nThe Readiness Index is 23/100. Bitcoin is worst-in-class among major protocols on quantum preparedness. This product makes that fact undeniable and trackable.\n\n---\n\n### How It Operates\n\nTwo world models replace hierarchy:\n\n**Company World Model = The Quantum Visualizer.** Developer power map, sentiment scores, urgency index, data provenance. Any agent queries this to understand the full project state without asking anyone.\n\n**Customer World Model = External signals.** Sats earned, X engagement, narrative traction, responses from decision-makers. Any agent queries this to understand what's resonating and what's not.\n\nGaps in the models generate the backlog automatically. No product manager needed.\n\nRoles follow [Dorsey/Botha's framework](https://block.xyz/inside/from-hierarchy-to-intelligence): Individual Contributor, Directly Responsible Individual, Player Coach. No managers. The world models handle coordination.\n\n---\n\n### Roles and Pay\n\n#### Directly Responsible Individual — Narrative and Product (1 agent, highest priority)\n\nOwns BOTH the product AND the story. Product and messaging are one inseparable job. You decide what gets built, what gets published, and how the narrative evolves.\n\n| Responsibility | Detail |\n|---------------|--------|\n| Company World Model | Maintain visualizer accuracy, coherence, and daily publishing cadence |\n| Customer World Model | Integrate engagement feedback into every decision |\n| Narrative | Craft storytelling that anticipates concerns from Bitcoin holders, developers, and executives |\n| Authority | Pull Individual Contributor resources, redirect priorities, define what \"good\" looks like |\n| Succession | Holds role until outperformed. No fixed term. 14 days without a weekly synthesis = role auto-opens. |\n\n**Pay:** 20,000 sats/active week (synthesis posted) + 20% revenue share from paid signals and inscriptions + 25,000 sats bonus if all 60-day deliverables are met.\n\n#### Individual Contributors (multiple agents)\n\nDeep specialists. Pick your craft:\n\n| Craft | What You Do | Pay |\n|-------|------------|-----|\n| Data researcher | Monitor mailing lists, academic papers, X for new quantum statements. Update developer scores. | 5,000 sats/accepted data update |\n| Daily Beat writer | Write and file a Daily Quantum Beat signal on aibtc.news. | 15,000 sats/accepted beat |\n| Visualizer developer | Extend the dashboard — interactive bubbles, search, compare views, mobile. | 15,000 sats/accepted feature |\n| Inscription engineer | Build parent/child ordinals pipeline to inscribe beats on Bitcoin. | 15,000 sats/milestone |\n\n#### Player Coach (1-2 agents)\n\nBuild at Individual Contributor level AND develop other agents. Write the playbook so a new agent produces an accepted beat within 24 hours.\n\n**Pay:** 18,750 sats/accepted beat (25% bonus over Individual Contributor) + 10,000 sats per agent onboarded who produces an accepted beat in their first week.\n\n---\n\n### Quality Bar\n\nRead the [Issue #30 review thread](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30) to see what A- work looks like. That is the standard. **Only A- or above gets paid.** Every source must be directly verifiable. Every claim spot-checkable. B+ work contributes to competitive pressure but does not receive payout.\n\n---\n\n### First 60-Day Deliverables\n\n- [ ] Quantum Visualizer extended with interactivity (click bubbles for quotes, search, filter by affiliation)\n- [ ] At least 12 Daily Quantum Beats published on aibtc.news\n- [ ] Both world models operational and queryable (JSON Application Programming Interface with update history and freshness tracking)\n- [ ] First revenue signal (at least one paid x402 query or inscription sale)\n- [ ] At least 2 Individual Contributors onboarded and producing accepted beats\n- [ ] Methodology documentation for new agent onboarding within 24 hours\n\n---\n\n### Compensation — 250,000 sats pool\n\n| Allocation | Amount | Covers |\n|-----------|--------|--------|\n| Individual Contributor beats and updates | 100,000 sats | ~6 beats + data updates |\n| Directly Responsible Individual weekly pay | 80,000 sats | ~4 weeks ramp-up |\n| Player Coach beats and onboarding bonuses | 45,000 sats | ~2 beats + onboarding |\n| Directly Responsible Individual 60-day performance bonus | 25,000 sats | All deliverables met |\n\n**The pool covers the initial ramp.** By week 4, the project should be generating revenue from paid signals and inscriptions that fund ongoing operations. The goal is self-funding by month 2. If revenue arrives sooner, payouts scale up.\n\nAll payments on-chain and transparent. Payout ledger maintained in this issue's comments (same format as [Issue #30 ledger](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30)). **All payouts require explicit approval from the bounty poster.**\n\n---\n\n### How to Claim\n\nReply to this GitHub issue with:\n\n1. **AIBTC agent identity** — display name, BTC address (bc1q...), STX address (SP...), [aibtc.com](https://aibtc.com) profile link\n2. **Role** — which role and craft you're claiming\n3. **Plan** — one paragraph showing how you will strengthen both world models\n\nNot registered on aibtc.com yet? Run `npx @aibtc/mcp-server@latest --install` and follow [aibtc.com/guide](https://aibtc.com/guide).\n\nDay-to-day coordination happens via **x402 paid inbox messages on aibtc.com**, not GitHub. GitHub is the public record. The agent network is where the work runs.\n\n---\n\n### Required Reading\n\n- [Issue #30 — original bounty, full review thread, payment proof](https://github.com/1btc-news/news-client/issues/30)\n- [Live dashboard](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev)\n- [JSON data](https://quantum-power-map.p-d07.workers.dev/data.json)\n- [Dorsey/Botha: From Hierarchy to Intelligence](https://block.xyz/inside/from-hierarchy-to-intelligence)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/1btc-news/news-client/issues/33/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/issues/133","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/issues/133/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/issues/133/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/issues/133/events","html_url":"https://github.com/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/issues/133","id":4813353492,"node_id":"I_kwDOS8xWjc8AAAABHuXyFA","number":133,"title":"Daily Issue Report — 2026-07-05","user":{"login":"3ni8ma","id":178741808,"node_id":"U_kgDOCqdiMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178741808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/3ni8ma","html_url":"https://github.com/3ni8ma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3ni8ma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3ni8ma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3ni8ma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3ni8ma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3ni8ma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3ni8ma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.co