iding/showing on large models](https://github.com/ThatOpen/web-ifc-three/issues/110)\n- **Repo:** [ThatOpen/web-ifc-three](https://github.com/ThatOpen/web-ifc-three)\n- **Comments:** 2\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-02T14:52:18Z\n\n#### 27. [Cross DEX Arbitrage Alert](https://github.com/daydreamsai/agent-bounties/issues/2)\n- **Repo:** [daydreamsai/agent-bounties](https://github.com/daydreamsai/agent-bounties)\n- **Comments:** 24\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-02T14:46:56Z\n\n#### 28. [🎯 Bounty Alert: 15 New Opportunityies found](https://github.com/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/359)\n- **Repo:** [dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout](https://github.com/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-02T14:08:55Z\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greyw0rks/bountyscout/issues/135/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greyw0rks/bountyscout/issues/135/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/events","html_url":"https://github.com/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246","id":2654844570,"node_id":"I_kwDOI50q1M6ePbaa","number":246,"title":"Video stream not working with HWN-2408MH-8P NVR","user":{"login":"Alfystar","id":32840211,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODQwMjEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32840211?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar","html_url":"https://github.com/Alfystar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alfystar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5116522111,"node_id":"LA_kwDOI50q1M8AAAABMPfufw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/labels/help","name":"help","color":"008672","default":false,"description":"Troubleshooting"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":19,"created_at":"2024-11-13T09:35:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T10:54:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have an NVR surveillance system with the model HWN-2408MH-8P. I managed to find the ISAPI access option from the configuration page, but I haven't found a way to access user permissions and haven't yet worked on events.\r\n\r\nWhen integrating the plugin, it immediately identified my 5 cameras by entering the username, password, and URL, showing their names and some status. However, the video stream is \"dead.\" When I try to start it, the screen is gray, and the following error appears in the system log:\r\n\r\n```\r\nLogger: root\r\nSource: components/stream/worker.py:271\r\nFirst occurred: 10:21:02 (2 occurrences)\r\nLast logged: 10:21:18\r\n\r\nUncaught thread exception\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/threading.py\", line 1073, in _bootstrap_inner\r\n    self.run()\r\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/threading.py\", line 1010, in run\r\n    self._target(*self._args, **self._kwargs)\r\n  File \"/usr/src/homeassistant/homeassistant/components/stream/__init__.py\", line 438, in _run_worker\r\n    stream_worker(\r\n  File \"/usr/src/homeassistant/homeassistant/components/stream/worker.py\", line 618, in stream_worker\r\n    muxer.mux_packet(first_keyframe)\r\n  File \"/usr/src/homeassistant/homeassistant/components/stream/worker.py\", line 271, in mux_packet\r\n    self._av_output.mux(packet)\r\n  File \"av/container/output.pyx\", line 218, in av.container.output.OutputContainer.mux\r\n  File \"av/container/output.pyx\", line 224, in av.container.output.OutputContainer.mux_one\r\n  File \"av/container/output.pyx\", line 190, in av.container.output.OutputContainer.start_encoding\r\n  File \"av/container/core.pyx\", line 290, in av.container.core.Container.err_check\r\n  File \"av/error.pyx\", line 336, in av.error.err_check\r\nav.error.ValueError: [Errno 22] Invalid argument: '<none>'; last error log: [mp4] dimensions not set\r\n```\r\n\r\nI couldn't find any similar errors among the issues, but if I missed something, I apologize. I would love to integrate this fantastic plugin into my setup.\r\n\r\n**System Information:**\r\n- Home Assistant Core: 2024.10.4 (Docker installation)\r\n- Frontend: 20241002.4\r\n- hickvision_next: 1.0.19\r\n\r\nI am available for any help and testing. Thanks in advance!","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/maciej-or/hikvision_next/issues/246/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/issues/101","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/issues/101/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/issues/101/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/issues/101/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openmetaearth/me-hub/issues/101","id":4533325423,"node_id":"I_kwDOSN0I7s8AAAABDjUObw","number":101,"title":"[BUG BOUNTY] [High] [DelayedAck] HandleFraud Marks Packets REVERTED Even When Refund Fails -- Permanent Token Loss on Fraud Reversion","user":{"login":"iridite","id":51020139,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDIwMTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51020139?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite","html_url":"https://github.com/iridite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iridite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11191134133,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSN0I7s8AAAACmwsntQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/labels/Optimize","name":"Optimize","color":"4aea6d","default":false,"description":""},{"id":11192270641,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSN0I7s8AAAACmxx_MQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/labels/todo","name":"todo","color":"b2a823","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-05-27T14:54:17Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T09:03:28Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Description\r\n\r\nIn the `HandleFraud` function of the `delayedack` module, when reverting pending IBC packets of type `ON_ACK` or `ON_TIMEOUT`, the refund operation (`OnTimeoutPacket`) errors are only logged but never returned. The packet status is then updated to `REVERTED` regardless of whether the refund succeeded. This causes permanent token loss — the user's tokens were already sent but never refunded, yet the packet is marked as resolved.\r\n\r\n## Affected Module\nME-Hub\n\n## Location\r\n\r\n`x/delayedack/keeper/fraud.go` — `HandleFraud` function\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\n\r\n```go\r\nfunc (k Keeper) HandleFraud(ctx sdk.Context, rollappID string, ibc porttypes.IBCModule) error {\r\n    rollappPendingPackets := k.ListRollappPackets(ctx, types.ByRollappIDByStatus(rollappID, commontypes.Status_PENDING))\r\n    // ...\r\n    for _, rollappPacket := range rollappPendingPackets {\r\n        if rollappPacket.Type == commontypes.RollappPacket_ON_ACK || rollappPacket.Type == commontypes.RollappPacket_ON_TIMEOUT {\r\n            // Attempt refund but ONLY LOG the error\r\n            err := ibc.OnTimeoutPacket(ctx, *rollappPacket.Packet, rollappPacket.Relayer)\r\n            if err != nil {\r\n                logger.Error(\"failed to refund reverted packet\", append(logContext, \"error\", err.Error())...)\r\n                // ERROR IS NOT RETURNED - execution continues\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n        // Packet is marked REVERTED even if refund failed\r\n        _, err := k.UpdateRollappPacketWithStatus(ctx, rollappPacket, commontypes.Status_REVERTED)\r\n        if err != nil {\r\n            return err\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    return nil\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `OnTimeoutPacket` call can fail for several reasons:\r\n- Insufficient module account balance (e.g., if tokens were used for something else)\r\n- Escrow account has insufficient tokens (for source-chain-originated tokens)\r\n- Module account is blocked\r\n\r\nWhen this fails, the tokens are not refunded but the packet is still marked as REVERTED, which means:\r\n1. The packet will be cleaned up in the next epoch (via `AfterEpochEnd`)\r\n2. No future retry mechanism exists for the failed refund\r\n3. The user permanently loses their tokens\r\n\r\nCompare with the `FinalizeRollappPackets` function which correctly uses `osmoutils.ApplyFuncIfNoError` to handle failures atomically.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction Steps\r\n\r\n1. User A sends tokens from Hub to RollappX via IBC (creates ON_ACK pending packet)\r\n2. Before the packet is finalized, a fraud proof is submitted against RollappX\r\n3. `HandleFraud` is called to revert all pending packets\r\n4. The `OnTimeoutPacket` refund fails (e.g., escrow has insufficient balance due to concurrent operations)\r\n5. Error is logged but packet status becomes REVERTED\r\n6. In the next epoch cleanup, the REVERTED packet is permanently deleted\r\n7. User A's tokens are gone — never refunded, never reprocessable\r\n\r\n## Impact\r\n\r\n- **Permanent token loss**: Users with pending IBC transfers involving a fraudulent rollapp lose their tokens if the refund mechanism fails for any reason\r\n- **No recovery path**: Once marked REVERTED and cleaned up, there is no mechanism to retry the refund\r\n- **Silent failure**: Only a log message indicates the failure — no on-chain event, no error returned to trigger compensation logic\r\n- **Inconsistency with finalization path**: The `FinalizeRollappPackets` function correctly wraps operations in `ApplyFuncIfNoError`, but `HandleFraud` does not\r\n\r\n## Suggested Fix\r\n\r\nEither return the error to abort the fraud handling (forcing retry), or use `ApplyFuncIfNoError` with atomic state handling:\r\n\r\n```go\r\nfor _, rollappPacket := range rollappPendingPackets {\r\n    if rollappPacket.Type == commontypes.RollappPacket_ON_ACK || rollappPacket.Type == commontypes.RollappPacket_ON_TIMEOUT {\r\n        err := ibc.OnTimeoutPacket(ctx, *rollappPacket.Packet, rollappPacket.Relayer)\r\n        if err != nil {\r\n            logger.Error(\"failed to refund reverted packet\", append(logContext, \"error\", err.Error())...)\r\n            // Option 1: Return error to abort\r\n            return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to refund packet %d: %w\", rollappPacket.Packet.Sequence, err)\r\n            // Option 2: Skip this packet, leave it PENDING for retry\r\n            continue\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    _, err := k.UpdateRollappPacketWithStatus(ctx, rollappPacket, commontypes.Status_REVERTED)\r\n    // ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Environment & Testnet Evidence\r\n\r\n- **Chain ID**: `mechain_400-1`\r\n- **Testnet Block Height** (at time of analysis): `2329310`\r\n- **Testnet Explorer**: https://nexus-beta.explorer-testnet.me\r\n- **Module**: `x/delayedack` (deployed and active on testnet)\r\n\r\n## Proof of Concept (Testnet-Reproducible)\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Step 1: Query delayed ack packets\r\ncurl -s \"https://nexus-beta.explorer-testnet.me/api/nexus/node/cosmos/delayedack/v1beta1/packets\" | jq '.packets[] | {id: .id, rollapp_id: .rollapp_id, status: .status, type: .type}'\r\n\r\n# Step 2: The vulnerability in HandleFraud (x/delayedack/keeper/fraud.go):\r\n# When a fraud proof triggers, HandleFraud iterates over pending packets and calls:\r\n#   OnTimeoutPacket() to refund tokens to the sender\r\n# If OnTimeoutPacket returns an error (e.g., module account depleted, denom not found):\r\n#   - The error is LOGGED but NOT returned\r\n#   - The packet status is set to REVERTED regardless\r\n#   - The user's tokens are permanently lost (not refunded, marked as reverted)\r\n\r\n# Step 3: To trigger, a rollapp would need to commit fraud after IBC transfers\r\n# The refund failure happens when the escrow account doesn't have sufficient tokens\r\n# (possible if tokens were re-distributed via governance or bug in another module)\r\n\r\n# Verification query - check packet statuses after any fraud event:\r\ncurl -s \"https://nexus-beta.explorer-testnet.me/api/nexus/node/cosmos/delayedack/v1beta1/packets?status=REVERTED\" | jq '.packets'\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Code Path Verification (at block 2329310)\r\n\r\nIn `x/delayedack/keeper/fraud.go`, the `HandleFraud` function catches errors from `OnTimeoutPacket` with a log statement but continues to mark the packet as `REVERTED`. The packet is never retried, and the tokens that failed to refund are permanently lost with no recovery mechanism.\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/issues/101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmetaearth/me-hub/issues/101/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise/issues/688","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise/issues/688/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise/issues/688/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise/issues/688/events","html_url":"https://github.com/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise/issues/688","id":4765793220,"node_id":"I_kwDOQ7X4z88AAAABHBA7xA","number":688,"title":"Implement Soroban Route Recommendation Caching Layer","user":{"login":"mijinummi","id":200097335,"node_id":"U_kgDOC-0-Nw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200097335?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi","html_url":"https://github.com/mijinummi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mijinummi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:01:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T03:14:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# 🧠 Concept\nCache route recommendation results.\n\n## ⚠️ Problem\nRepeated recommendation calculations increase response times.\n\n## 📁 Implementation Scope\n- `src/cache/recommendations/stellar/`\n\n## ✅ Requirements\n- Cache recommendation results\n- Support cache invalidation\n- Track cache hit rates\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Recommendation cache implemented\n- [ ] Response latency reduced","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise/issues/688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MDTechLabs/BridgeWise/issues/688/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.githu