tps://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/labels/automated-report","name":"automated-report","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-01T17:28:56Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T17:28:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Daily Issue Discovery — 2026-07-01\n\nFound **15** open issues matching your stack.\n\n| # | Repo | Issue | Labels |\n|---|------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | RatLoopz/sahidawa-india | [Feat : Interactive Modal to Request OCR Verification for Unverified Medicines#2891](https://github.com/RatLoopz/sahidawa-india/pull/2935) | level:advanced, quality:clean, gssoc:approved, type:feature, good first issue, status: open-for-all |\n| 2 | naborajs/birthday-bloom | [docs: Add screenshots/GIFs showing how to customize the birthday page](https://github.com/naborajs/birthday-bloom/issues/29) | documentation, good first issue |\n| 3 | RatLoopz/sahidawa-india | [fix(i18n): localize Footer, add fallback messages and test fixes](https://github.com/RatLoopz/sahidawa-india/pull/2932) | level:intermediate, quality:clean, gssoc:approved, type:bug, good first issue |\n| 4 | 123a-bcd/nailstorm-bounty-forge-358 | [[$50 BOUNTY] [Go] Limit analytics metric tag cardinality](https://github.com/123a-bcd/nailstorm-bounty-forge-358/issues/14) | help wanted, good first issue, bounty, language:go |\n| 5 | ronisarkarexe/story-spark-ai | [test : add unit tests for useKeyboardShortcuts hook](https://github.com/ronisarkarexe/story-spark-ai/issues/4609) | good first issue, gssoc26, gssoc, type:testing, gssoc'26, type:refactor |\n| 6 | docsifyjs/docsify | [Keyboard focus is getting lost after activating home control in left navigation pane in windows.](https://github.com/docsifyjs/docsify/issues/2600) | bug, good first Issue, accessibility, v5-rc |\n| 7 | viru0909-dev/nyay-setu-working | [feat(nlp): add semantic Redis cache for legal queries](https://github.com/viru0909-dev/nyay-setu-working/pull/1500) | good first issue, level:advanced, quality:exceptional, gssoc:approved, type:feature, type:testing, type:security, type:performance |\n| 8 | shamilahmdt/devtasks | [🟢 Good First Issue: Add Git Command Builder & Scenario Solver to Dev Utilities](https://github.com/shamilahmdt/devtasks/issues/340) | enhancement, help wanted, good first issue, ui, workflow, Beginner Friendly |\n| 9 | Ayushh-Sharmaa/NexaSphere | [[BUG]: Missing Lazy Loading and Image Optimization for Directory and Event Assets](https://github.com/Ayushh-Sharmaa/NexaSphere/issues/2959) | bug, good first issue, GSSoC'26, level:beginner, NSOC'26, mentor:Ayushh-Sharmaa, priority:medium, needs-more-info, needs-labels, assigned, website |\n| 10 | AI-First-Community/Bodhi | [PWA: add a maskable app icon](https://github.com/AI-First-Community/Bodhi/issues/6) | good first issue |\n| 11 | kubeflow/sdk | [Document how to use `options` with TrainerClient](https://github.com/kubeflow/sdk/issues/388) | good first issue, help wanted, area/docs |\n| 12 | sblunt/orbitize | [Multinest tutorial & install instructions](https://github.com/sblunt/orbitize/issues/405) | enhancement, help wanted, good first issue, easy |\n| 13 | maziyarpanahi/openmed | [Build the HPO phenotype linker for clinical-finding spans](https://github.com/maziyarpanahi/openmed/issues/297) | help wanted, good first issue, roadmap-v2, feature, P2 |\n| 14 | digitalfabrik/integreat-cms | [Position block in the POI form overflows](https://github.com/digitalfabrik/integreat-cms/issues/4401) | good first issue, feature:Places/Map |\n| 15 | saleor/saleor | [Provide better message for transactionAPI](https://github.com/saleor/saleor/issues/13951) | good first issue, transactionAPI |\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/issues/83/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/3ni8ma/aarushkarak-website/issues/83/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft/issues/159","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft/issues/159/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft/issues/159/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft/issues/159/events","html_url":"https://github.com/unitaryfoundation/clifft/issues/159","id":4786614379,"node_id":"I_kwDOSD1gp88AAAABHU3waw","number":159,"title":"Productionize an opt-in phase-polynomial T-count pass","user":{"login":"bachase","id":14430,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase","html_url":"https://github.com/bachase","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bachase/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10704799427,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSD1gp88AAAACfg5Gww","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-01T14:46:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T14:48:31Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem or motivation\n\nIssue #40 explored HIR-level global T-count optimization as a UnitaryHACK prototype task. PR #132 showed that a phase-polynomial / TOHPE-style HIR pass can reduce T count beyond the existing peephole pass on some dense phase-polynomial circuit families, while remaining opt-in and avoiding HIR, bytecode, and VM layout changes.\n\nThat work was useful as a scientific prototype, but it is not ready to merge as-is. To include this kind of pass in Clifft, it should be reworked as a production-quality contribution rather than a hackathon proof of concept.\n\nThe follow-up should preserve the useful result from the prototype while removing the POC framing, tightening the implementation, and rewriting the documentation in the style of the existing Clifft docs.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nCreate a new PR that productionizes an opt-in HIR T-count optimization pass based on the #132 prototype.\n\nThe pass should remain experimental / opt-in and should not be added to the default optimization pipeline in this issue.\n\nExpected scope:\n\n- Keep the implementation inside the existing HIR optimization layer.\n- Do not change the parser, HIR layout, bytecode format, VM instruction format, or VM memory model.\n- Do not add new third-party C++ dependencies without prior maintainer discussion.\n- Keep the pass `default_enabled = false`.\n- Preserve correctness for circuits where the pass does not apply.\n- Preserve source-map behavior where feasible, and document any synthesized-operation provenance policy clearly in code/tests.\n\n### Documentation\n\nReplace the prototype documentation with fresh project documentation.\n\nThe new docs should stand alone as user/developer documentation for an opt-in Clifft pass. They should not read as a continuation of the hackathon submission, a reviewer response, or a benchmark report.\n\nA good shape would be one concise documentation page, or a short tutorial plus the normal pass reference entry, covering:\n\n- what the pass does;\n- when it may be useful;\n- how to enable it from Python / pass managers;\n- its important limitations;\n- the prior work it relies on, with citations;\n- one small runnable example;\n- how correctness is tested at a high level.\n\nAvoid carrying over the current prototype docs verbatim. In particular, do not include bounty/hackathon framing, self-review checklists, long exploratory benchmark narratives, or LLM-style explanatory prose. Benchmark evidence can be summarized briefly if it helps users understand when the pass is useful, but detailed exploratory tables should not replace tests or concise documentation.\n\nThe tone should match existing docs such as `docs/guide/compilation.md`, `docs/reference/passes.md`, and `docs/theory/architecture.md`.\n\n### Implementation quality\n\nThe implementation should be reviewed and simplified for production quality.\n\nPlease pay particular attention to:\n\n- clear pass boundaries and names;\n- idiomatic C++20 matching nearby optimizer code;\n- concise comments that explain non-obvious invariants or algorithmic choices, not step-by-step narration;\n- avoiding stale \"phase A / phase B\" or prototype-planning language unless it directly names a real algorithmic stage;\n- reusing existing helpers such as `MaskView`, `MutableMaskView`, `anti_commute`, `can_swap`, and existing pass-manager conventions where appropriate;\n- bounding compile-time search costs with explicit, tested limits;\n- making any dependence on a following pass explicit. A pass may benefit from a later `PeepholeFusionPass`, but emitted HIR should remain semantically valid on its own.\n\nIf any benchmark or developer tool remains, it should be small, maintainable, and clearly separated from the user-facing docs.\n\n### Testing\n\nAdd robust tests that justify merging this as an opt-in pass.\n\nAt minimum, the PR should include:\n\n- focused unit tests for the reducer / phase-polynomial logic;\n- HIR pass tests for cases that reduce T count;\n- no-op tests for sparse, unsupported, or above-limit cases;\n- semantic-equivalence tests for circuits where the pass changes the program;\n- tests covering any residual `PHASE_ROTATION` behavior, both with and without a following peephole pass if relevant;\n- source-map regression tests for rewritten blocks;\n- Python binding / pass-manager tests if the pass is exposed to Python;\n- default-pipeline regression coverage showing existing optimization behavior is unchanged.\n\nSmall statevector or dense-unitary checks are appropriate for reduced examples. Larger examples may use exact phase-function checks or another clearly justified oracle, but any changed program should have some correctness evidence.\n\nThe submitted PR should pass:\n\n- `ctest --test-dir build -E Bench --output-on-failure`\n- `uv run pytest tests/python/ -v`\n- `uv run pytest --codeblocks docs/ README.md -v`\n- `uv run pre-commit run --all-files`\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The pass is opt-in and registered consistently with existing pass infrastructure.\n- The implementation is scoped to HIR optimization and does not change parser, HIR layout, bytecode, or VM structures.\n- The code is production-quality C++/Python in the style of the surrounding project.\n- The docs are freshly written in Clifft's documentation style and do not carry over prototype or hackathon framing.\n- The docs clearly cite the algorithmic prior work and accurately describe the implemented subset.\n- The pass demonstrates at least one meaningful T-count reduction beyond `PeepholeFusionPass` on a representative structured circuit family.\n- Every evaluated changed circuit has a corresponding semantic-equivalence check where feasible.\n- Limits and skipped cases are explicit, tested, and documented.\n- Existing tests and pre-commit checks pass.\n- The PR includes a short conclusion in the PR description explaining what was productionized from #132, what was intentionally dropped, and what remains future work.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\nLeave #132 open as an exploratory prototype. That preserves the hackathon work, but it mixes useful implementation ideas with POC documentation, exploratory benchmarking, and review-specific framing.\n\nMerge #132 as-is but keep the pass opt-in. This would add useful experimental functionality, but it would also make later maintenance harder because the docs and implementation still need production cleanup.\n\nDo not add a T-count pass for now. That remains an option if the productionized version cannot meet the correctness, clarity, and maintainability bar, but #132 showed enough promise to justify a focused follow-up.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft/issues/159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/unitaryfoundation/clifft/issues/159/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/96","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/96/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/96/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/96/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/96","id":2878024403,"node_id":"I_kwDONlDJhc6riyrT","number":96,"title":"Local Model Support via Ollama $400","user":{"login":"rparcus","id":923630,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMzYzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/923630?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus","html_url":"https://github.com/rparcus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7954718512,"node_id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB2iNfMA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"},{"id":8203667011,"node_id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6PoGQw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"395808","default":false,"description":""},{"id":8204009529,"node_id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6P9AOQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/labels/llm","name":"llm","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Issues related to LLM integrations and features"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":17,"created_at":"2025-02-25T11:06:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T11:48:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"ty